  "question": {
    "text": "The molecular formula of a commercial resin used for exchanging ions in water softening is <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>molecular</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>weight</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>206</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. What would be the maximum uptake of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> ions by the resin if expressed in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mol</mi></math> per <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>gm</mi></math>?",
